    <statement><p><p>The table shows the resting heart rates, in beats per minute (bpm), of <m>{41}</m> Grade 12 learners.</p><tabular border="1" style="border-collapse:collapse;text-align:center;"><row><cell style="padding:4px 10px;">Heart rate (bpm) (<m>x</m>)</cell><cell style="padding:4px 10px;"><m>{63}</m></cell><cell style="padding:4px 10px;"><m>{64}</m></cell><cell style="padding:4px 10px;"><m>{65}</m></cell><cell style="padding:4px 10px;"><m>{66}</m></cell><cell style="padding:4px 10px;"><m>{67}</m></cell><cell style="padding:4px 10px;"><m>{68}</m></cell></row><row><cell style="padding:4px 10px;">Number of learners (<m>f</m>)</cell><cell style="padding:4px 10px;"><m>{3}</m></cell><cell style="padding:4px 10px;"><m>{4}</m></cell><cell style="padding:4px 10px;"><m>{8}</m></cell><cell style="padding:4px 10px;"><m>{14}</m></cell><cell style="padding:4px 10px;"><m>{10}</m></cell><cell style="padding:4px 10px;"><m>{2}</m></cell></row></tabular><p>Use the assumed mean <m>A = {66}</m>, with <m>d = x - A</m>.</p><p>(a) Find <m>\Sigma fd</m>.</p><div><m>\Sigma fd =</m> <fillin characters="5" name="ans1"/>  </div><p>(b) Find <m>\Sigma fd^2</m>.</p><div><m>\Sigma fd^2 =</m> <fillin characters="5" name="ans2"/>  </div><p>(c) Find the mean, correct to 1 decimal place.</p><div><m>\bar{x} =</m> <fillin characters="6" name="ans3"/>  </div><p>(d) Find the standard deviation, correct to 2 decimal places.</p><div><m>\sigma =</m> <fillin characters="6" name="ans4"/>  </div></p></statement>
    <solution><p><p>Subtracting the same number <m>A</m> from every value moves the mean down by <m>A</m> and leaves the spread unchanged. So work with the small deviations <m>d = x - A</m>: add <m>A</m> back to their mean, but not to their standard deviation, because the variance of <m>x</m> equals the variance of <m>d</m>.</p><tabular border="1" style="border-collapse:collapse;text-align:center;"><row><cell style="padding:4px 10px;"><m>x</m></cell><cell style="padding:4px 10px;"><m>{63}</m></cell><cell style="padding:4px 10px;"><m>{64}</m></cell><cell style="padding:4px 10px;"><m>{65}</m></cell><cell style="padding:4px 10px;"><m>{66}</m></cell><cell style="padding:4px 10px;"><m>{67}</m></cell><cell style="padding:4px 10px;"><m>{68}</m></cell><cell style="padding:4px 10px;">Total</cell></row><row><cell style="padding:4px 10px;"><m>f</m></cell><cell style="padding:4px 10px;"><m>{3}</m></cell><cell style="padding:4px 10px;"><m>{4}</m></cell><cell style="padding:4px 10px;"><m>{8}</m></cell><cell style="padding:4px 10px;"><m>{14}</m></cell><cell style="padding:4px 10px;"><m>{10}</m></cell><cell style="padding:4px 10px;"><m>{2}</m></cell><cell style="padding:4px 10px;"><m>{41}</m></cell></row><row><cell style="padding:4px 10px;"><m>d = x - {66}</m></cell><cell style="padding:4px 10px;"><m>{-3}</m></cell><cell style="padding:4px 10px;"><m>{-2}</m></cell><cell style="padding:4px 10px;"><m>{-1}</m></cell><cell style="padding:4px 10px;"><m>{0}</m></cell><cell style="padding:4px 10px;"><m>{1}</m></cell><cell style="padding:4px 10px;"><m>{2}</m></cell><cell style="padding:4px 10px;"/></row><row><cell style="padding:4px 10px;"><m>fd</m></cell><cell style="padding:4px 10px;"><m>{-9}</m></cell><cell style="padding:4px 10px;"><m>{-8}</m></cell><cell style="padding:4px 10px;"><m>{-8}</m></cell><cell style="padding:4px 10px;"><m>{0}</m></cell><cell style="padding:4px 10px;"><m>{10}</m></cell><cell style="padding:4px 10px;"><m>{4}</m></cell><cell style="padding:4px 10px;"><m>{-11}</m></cell></row><row><cell style="padding:4px 10px;"><m>fd^2</m></cell><cell style="padding:4px 10px;"><m>{27}</m></cell><cell style="padding:4px 10px;"><m>{16}</m></cell><cell style="padding:4px 10px;"><m>{8}</m></cell><cell style="padding:4px 10px;"><m>{0}</m></cell><cell style="padding:4px 10px;"><m>{10}</m></cell><cell style="padding:4px 10px;"><m>{8}</m></cell><cell style="padding:4px 10px;"><m>{69}</m></cell></row></tabular><p>(a) <m>\Sigma fd = {-11}</m>. (b) <m>\Sigma fd^2 = {69}</m>.</p><p>(c) <me>\bar{x} = A + \frac{\Sigma fd}{\Sigma f} = {66} - \frac{ {11} }{ {41} } \approx {65.7}</me></p><p>(d) <me>\sigma^2 = \frac{\Sigma fd^2}{\Sigma f} - \left(\frac{\Sigma fd}{\Sigma f}\right)^2 = \frac{ {69} }{ {41} } - \left(\frac{ {-11} }{ {41} }\right)^2 \approx {1.611}</me>so <m>\sigma = \sqrt{\sigma^2} \approx {1.27}</m>, using the unrounded variance.</p></p></solution>
    <answer><p><m>-11</m></p></answer>
    <answer><p><m>69</m></p></answer>
    <answer><p><m>\frac{2695}{41}</m></p></answer>
    <answer><p><m>\frac{2 \sqrt{677}}{41}</m></p></answer>
</stack-static>